# Search scope for ripgrep (and so for agent Grep/Glob). Git does not read this file.
#
# `.sdlc/` is a hidden directory, and ripgrep skips hidden directories by default, so the
# SDLC's own config, scripts and templates would drop out of every search without this line.
!.sdlc/
#
# Archived specs stay tracked in git but out of default search. A spec is written in
# future tense and never rewritten, so once it closes its description of the system keeps
# reading as current; position is what keeps it out of an agent's way. Reach it by id with
# `node .sdlc/scripts/resolve.mjs SPEC-NNN`, or search with `rg --no-ignore`.
specs/archive/
